WEBVTT

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:14.620
"Stage 2
'Ouija Exchange'
Grant the spirit's three wishes
and obtain 'Chromosome 01.'"

00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:18.870
"Yes"      "No"

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:25.870
For them to progress this far
so smoothly... I'm impressed.

00:00:25.870 --> 00:00:30.290
Perhaps that's saying how talented they are?

00:00:30.290 --> 00:00:35.870
Now then, it's about time
for the real fun to begin.

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:55.290
Do you think Makino might have a girlfriend?

00:00:56.370 --> 00:00:58.000
Whoa! Watch it!

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:00.330
Huh? What do you mean?

00:01:00.330 --> 00:01:02.620
Well, I don't know for sure, but...

00:01:02.620 --> 00:01:05.580
This morning, when Himiko
and I went to wake him...

00:01:06.790 --> 00:01:08.450
Makino!

00:01:08.450 --> 00:01:10.790
Makino! It's morning!

00:01:10.790 --> 00:01:13.330
Your bonito flake rice is waiting!

00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:17.660
It's bonito flake rice!

00:01:18.700 --> 00:01:21.200
Thank you, Sumire.

00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:25.450
"Thump Thump"
And, well, something adorable happened.

00:01:25.450 --> 00:01:29.040
Is that why she's been as red
as a lobster since morning?

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:31.950
Sumire? Are you sure that's not a pet of his?

00:01:31.950 --> 00:01:35.120
No, I think his pet cat was named Moshika.

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:39.620
"Eek"
I bet Makimaki has a lover or two.
Or maybe five or six!

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:42.080
"Eek"
S-Six timing is bad!

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:44.370
Girls can't resist love gossip.

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:46.580
Iride's in there though.

00:01:46.580 --> 00:01:48.540
That doesn't even seem odd.

00:01:49.790 --> 00:01:53.500
By the way, is there anyone
among us who's dating someone?

00:01:53.660 --> 00:01:54.700
"Silence"

00:01:56.700 --> 00:01:58.830
Oh? Wipeout?

00:01:58.830 --> 00:02:00.870
"Girlfriend"
What's a girlfriend?

00:02:00.870 --> 00:02:02.200
"Girlfriend"
Is it tasty?

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:04.200
"Girlfriend"
Are they sold at the convenience store?

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:05.660
"Girlfriend"
Shall I warm it up?

00:02:05.660 --> 00:02:08.120
"Girlfriend"
All right, my bad. Cut it out.

00:02:08.120 --> 00:02:10.830
I go to an all-girls school, so...

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:12.870
But some girls had boyfriends...

00:02:12.870 --> 00:02:14.950
I go to an all-boys school, too.

00:02:14.950 --> 00:02:16.830
Though some had girlfriends...

00:02:17.910 --> 00:02:20.620
Engaging in romance before
a marital blood oath?!

00:02:20.620 --> 00:02:23.410
That's so carnal... and depraved!

00:02:23.410 --> 00:02:24.910
B-Blood oath?

00:02:24.910 --> 00:02:26.450
How idiotic.

00:02:28.950 --> 00:02:31.750
Excuse me? In that case, what about you?!

00:02:31.750 --> 00:02:34.700
Huh?! I've got no interest in girls!

00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:36.700
Go figure, you kindergartner!

00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:38.790
Shuddap, Taisho period!

00:02:38.790 --> 00:02:39.660
Meiji period!

00:02:39.660 --> 00:02:41.540
Yayoi period!

00:02:41.540 --> 00:02:45.080
--Ooh, Makimaki! Let's ask him!
--You skipped too much, idiot!

00:02:45.080 --> 00:02:47.290
Who is this Sumire?

00:02:51.790 --> 00:02:53.660
He's got a girlfriend then?!

00:02:53.660 --> 00:02:55.450
That's Makino for you!

00:02:56.950 --> 00:02:59.370
"Makino stocks mysteriously rise"

00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:16.040
I wonder what kind of person
Makino's girlfriend is.

00:03:16.040 --> 00:03:20.000
If he confused Himiko and her,
I bet she's younger than him.

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:22.080
Older.

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:27.330
That look on his face was like someone
being spoiled by an older girlfriend.

00:03:28.910 --> 00:03:31.830
In that case, let's settle it with a vote.

00:03:31.830 --> 00:03:36.080
What's the point of deciding his
girlfriend's age by a majority vote?

00:03:36.080 --> 00:03:38.000
All right, here we go!

00:03:42.040 --> 00:03:45.040
Who thinks she's younger?

00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:46.330
Who thinks she's older?

00:03:46.330 --> 00:03:47.330
Me!

00:03:50.120 --> 00:03:51.120
Me!

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:55.160
♪ Ding dong, ding neigh! ♪

00:03:57.370 --> 00:04:02.040
Thank you for gathering today, everyone.

00:04:02.040 --> 00:04:04.580
Next up is Game 10, right?

00:04:04.580 --> 00:04:06.620
That was the plan, but...

00:04:06.620 --> 00:04:11.370
Before that, I have prepared something
special for everyone to enjoy.

00:04:11.370 --> 00:04:12.870
Something special?!

00:04:12.870 --> 00:04:16.120
You moron. Don't take
what he says at face value.

00:04:16.120 --> 00:04:17.870
You'll regret getting worked up.

00:04:17.870 --> 00:04:20.870
He's probably having us
do something dumb again.

00:04:20.870 --> 00:04:24.120
Well then, let us begin.

00:04:25.330 --> 00:04:29.040
Paka's Island!

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:32.290
As a reward for progressing
this far in the game,

00:04:32.290 --> 00:04:37.040
I would like for all of you to
participate in this bonus stage!

00:04:40.250 --> 00:04:42.830
Is this really just something to enjoy?

00:04:42.830 --> 00:04:49.540
Of course! Don't bonus stages go
hand in hand with RPGs and the like?

00:04:49.540 --> 00:04:51.620
That explains these outfits...

00:04:51.620 --> 00:04:54.660
"Pipes" "Card Room" "Slot Room"
"Coin Exchange"
"Battlefield" "Elevator Hall" "Dice Game"
I will be distributing a number of coins

00:04:54.660 --> 00:04:56.000
"Pipes" "Card Room" "Slot Room"
"Coin Exchange"
"Battlefield" "Elevator Hall" "Dice Game"
to each of you.

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:58.000
"Pipes" "Card Room" "Slot Room"
"Coin Exchange"
"Battlefield" "Elevator Hall" "Dice Game"
With these coins, you are to play

00:04:58.000 --> 00:04:59.330
"Pipes" "Card Room" "Slot Room"
"Coin Exchange"
"Battlefield" "Elevator Hall" "Dice Game"
any game of your choice...

00:04:59.330 --> 00:05:02.580
"Pipes" "Card Room" "Slot Room"
"Coin Exchange"
"Battlefield" "Elevator Hall" "Dice Game"
...and attempt to earn more before time runs out.

00:05:02.580 --> 00:05:04.330
"Pipes" "Card Room" "Slot Room"
"Coin Exchange"
"Battlefield" "Elevator Hall" "Dice Game"
Woohoo!

00:05:04.330 --> 00:05:06.910
Using all the coins that everyone gathers,

00:05:06.910 --> 00:05:12.000
you can trade in for wonderful
prizes at the Coin Exchange!

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:13.200
Coin Exchange?

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:15.080
What kind of prizes are there?

00:05:15.330 --> 00:05:16.950
"Paka Headband"   "Paka Pajamas"

00:05:16.950 --> 00:05:18.910
"Canned Paka"                        "Paka Parka"

00:05:19.160 --> 00:05:21.000
Ooh!

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:25.200
Paka Headband! Paka Pajamas!
Paka Parka! Canned Paka!

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:26.870
What do you think?!

00:05:26.870 --> 00:05:30.700
Tons of rare goods! Popular stuff
from the past! Rereleases!

00:05:30.700 --> 00:05:33.790
The finest picks you could ever imagine!

00:05:33.790 --> 00:05:37.370
That's pretty demotivating
for everyone except the moron.

00:05:37.370 --> 00:05:39.080
What are you talking about?

00:05:39.080 --> 00:05:43.200
It's a lineup good enough
to make any collector salivate.

00:05:43.200 --> 00:05:45.200
"Make Any Request Come True Ticket"
Huh? That's...

00:05:45.200 --> 00:05:47.950
"Make Any Request Come True Ticket"
"Make Any Request Come True Ticket"?

00:05:47.950 --> 00:05:50.500
"Make Any Request Come True Ticket"
As the name implies, if you earn this,

00:05:50.500 --> 00:05:55.750
I will grant any single request
that you wish to come true.

00:05:56.910 --> 00:06:04.540
Of course, it must be a wish confined to
<i>The Ones Within</i>, but that's the only condition.

00:06:06.370 --> 00:06:11.200
Anyway, with this being a bonus stage
and all, let's all try to enjoy it!

00:06:11.200 --> 00:06:14.620
Now then, your time limit is 120 minutes.

00:06:14.620 --> 00:06:18.330
You may earn as many coins
as you please within that time.

00:06:18.330 --> 00:06:22.450
Everyone, I wish you the best of luck!

00:06:27.830 --> 00:06:29.000
Low.

00:06:33.750 --> 00:06:35.330
Woohoo!

00:06:35.330 --> 00:06:39.910
Looks like you're doing well, Karin.
How many do you have now?

00:06:43.040 --> 00:06:45.660
Wh-What? Got a problem?

00:06:45.660 --> 00:06:48.000
N-No! What game is this?

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:50.250
It seems like High-Lo.

00:06:50.250 --> 00:06:53.040
It's a simple game
where you get dealt a card...

00:06:53.040 --> 00:06:56.620
...and guess if it's higher or
lower than the dealer's card.

00:06:58.080 --> 00:07:02.540
You double your coins if you
get it right and can quit or continue.

00:07:02.540 --> 00:07:03.950
But, Karin...

00:07:03.950 --> 00:07:08.750
If you always only bet one coin and
don't continue, you'll never get more.

00:07:08.750 --> 00:07:11.790
Shut up, okay? It's better than losing them.

00:07:18.040 --> 00:07:20.410
I lost one already...

00:07:20.410 --> 00:07:25.080
The fainthearted who can't bet more
than one coin aren't suited for gambling.

00:07:25.080 --> 00:07:28.830
It's people like you who don't think
of consequences and the future...

00:07:28.830 --> 00:07:30.830
...that aren't suited for gambling.

00:07:30.830 --> 00:07:32.830
You just don't get it.

00:07:32.830 --> 00:07:36.500
Gambling is all or nothing.
Win big or lose big.

00:07:36.500 --> 00:07:39.750
Leaving everything up to fate
is the romance of it all.

00:07:41.080 --> 00:07:43.540
A high schooler shouldn't idolize gambling.

00:07:43.540 --> 00:07:45.120
My bro Ken said that.

00:07:45.120 --> 00:07:46.080
Stealing his lines?!

00:07:46.080 --> 00:07:48.080
Huh?! You wanna piece?!

00:07:48.080 --> 00:07:51.290
Bring it. Let's settle this
before the game ends.

00:07:59.330 --> 00:08:02.080
I get where Anboy's coming from though.

00:08:02.080 --> 00:08:05.250
I'm not interested in paltry winnings either.

00:08:05.250 --> 00:08:08.250
It's time to go big or go home.

00:08:10.580 --> 00:08:12.080
"Mimicry Man-eater A has appeared!"

00:08:12.080 --> 00:08:13.500
"Mimicry Man-eater A has appeared!"
"Mimicry Man-eater B has appeared!"

00:08:13.500 --> 00:08:15.000
"Mimicry Man-eater B has appeared!"
"Mimicry Man-eater C has appeared!"

00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:16.910
"Mimicry Man-eater C has appeared!"
"Punitsuki has appeared!"

00:08:16.910 --> 00:08:20.750
"Mimicry Man-eater A"
"Mimicry Man-eater B"
"Mimicry Man-eater C" "Punitsuki"
We've just gotta go with our gut. All in on A!

00:08:20.750 --> 00:08:23.120
"Mimicry Man-eater A"
"Mimicry Man-eater B"
"Mimicry Man-eater C" "Punitsuki"
I'm going all in on Punitsuki.

00:08:23.120 --> 00:08:24.580
Are you in, Makimaki?

00:08:24.580 --> 00:08:26.950
Three thousand points on Taira Hara.

00:08:26.950 --> 00:08:29.000
All right, let's have at it!

00:08:36.500 --> 00:08:40.290
What the hell? This makes it
hard to cheer 'em on!

00:08:50.040 --> 00:08:52.250
Why am I the one getting beat up?!

00:08:52.250 --> 00:08:55.500
C'mon! Hang in there, Mimicry Man-eater B!

00:08:55.500 --> 00:09:01.290
--Anboy? Didn't you bet everything
on Mimicry Man-eater A?
--Get 'em! Fight back! Show those
jerks what we're made of!

00:09:05.250 --> 00:09:06.290
--Hell yeah!

00:09:06.290 --> 00:09:09.540
--Anboy? Do you not get the rules?
--Hell yeah!

00:09:10.540 --> 00:09:11.750
See that?!

00:09:11.750 --> 00:09:12.870
--Yeah, I did. I saw the true
depths of your stupidity.

00:09:12.870 --> 00:09:15.830
--Yeah, I did. I saw the true
depths of your stupidity.
--Yeah! Yeah! Woohoo!

00:09:15.830 --> 00:09:20.830
Let's say we lost the battle
but won the war, Zak.

00:09:20.830 --> 00:09:24.830
Like I said, gambling's all about
big wins and big losses.

00:09:24.830 --> 00:09:26.750
At this rate, I'll just have to extort
some coins from that furball.

00:09:26.750 --> 00:09:29.000
"Struggle" "Struggle"
At this rate, I'll just have to extort
some coins from that furball.

00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:32.000
"Struggle" "Struggle"
Huh, don'tcha got some?! Out with it already!

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:33.750
"Struggle" "Struggle"
Neigh...

00:09:33.750 --> 00:09:34.700
Let's go.

00:09:34.700 --> 00:09:37.540
Can we stop the violence, please?

00:09:37.540 --> 00:09:41.080
Fine, but quit smiling while holding that.

00:09:41.080 --> 00:09:43.910
You've got a lot of your coins left, Himi.

00:09:43.910 --> 00:09:46.160
What game have you been playing?

00:09:46.160 --> 00:09:49.450
None. I'm not very good at gambling, so...

00:09:49.450 --> 00:09:53.000
...I've just been watching people play.

00:09:53.000 --> 00:09:55.290
I-If you want some, help yourself!

00:09:55.290 --> 00:09:57.660
I probably won't end up using them!

00:09:57.660 --> 00:09:59.620
Yeah? Thanks.

00:09:59.620 --> 00:10:02.870
Himi is a definite people supporter, meow.

00:10:04.080 --> 00:10:08.580
Most of these games are straight
out of an RPG casino, but..

00:10:08.580 --> 00:10:09.620
Hmm?

00:10:12.250 --> 00:10:13.660
Pipes?

00:10:13.660 --> 00:10:15.330
This is clearly out of place.

00:10:15.330 --> 00:10:16.950
--Let's see...
--W-Wait!

00:10:16.950 --> 00:10:20.330
Learn how the game works
before you jump in!

00:10:20.330 --> 00:10:26.200
Oshigiri. You must be the type of person who
reads the manual before you play a game.

00:10:26.200 --> 00:10:28.620
I study it while on the toilet.

00:10:28.620 --> 00:10:31.750
I learn by doing rather than reading.

00:10:31.750 --> 00:10:33.040
Onigasaki!

00:10:40.830 --> 00:10:43.580
This is...

00:10:43.580 --> 00:10:47.580
It's been quite a while since Kai disappeared.

00:10:47.580 --> 00:10:49.620
This is why I told him to wait.

00:10:49.620 --> 00:10:52.540
It's Kai we're talking about, so any minute...

00:11:00.330 --> 00:11:01.620
He's back!

00:11:01.620 --> 00:11:06.700
Kaikoku, that's awesome!
You came back as Super Kai!

00:11:06.700 --> 00:11:08.040
Oy...

00:11:45.540 --> 00:11:47.250
A real dice game?

00:11:47.250 --> 00:11:50.580
I think only one person can play at a time.

00:11:50.580 --> 00:11:52.830
Okay, I'll give it a shot!

00:11:53.580 --> 00:11:55.790
"Dice Game"

00:11:58.330 --> 00:12:02.370
One, two, three, four, five, six.

00:12:03.370 --> 00:12:06.950
Ooh, Pandarou! Long time no see!

00:12:07.080 --> 00:12:08.700
"You reunite with Pandarou.
Advance 3."

00:12:08.700 --> 00:12:11.200
"You reunite with Pandarou.
Advance 3."
What a great start for me!

00:12:11.200 --> 00:12:13.000
One, two, three.

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:13.450
"Battlefield"

00:12:13.950 --> 00:12:15.620
"Battlefield"?

00:12:21.330 --> 00:12:24.500
"Punitsuki has appeared!"
Those three steps threw him straight into battle.

00:12:24.500 --> 00:12:27.040
"Punitsuki has appeared!"
Was that good luck or bad luck?

00:12:27.040 --> 00:12:30.410
It's like a family showdown or something.

00:12:30.410 --> 00:12:32.160
"Punitsuki calls for allies!"
Puni!

00:12:32.160 --> 00:12:33.660
"Punitsuki B has appeared!"
Puni!

00:12:33.660 --> 00:12:35.160
"Punitsuki C has appeared!"
Puni!

00:12:35.160 --> 00:12:36.700
"Punitsuki D has appeared!"
Puni!

00:12:36.700 --> 00:12:38.200
"Punitsuki E has appeared!"
Puni!

00:12:38.200 --> 00:12:39.700
"Punitsuki F has appeared!"
But it's calling for backup though!

00:12:39.700 --> 00:12:40.410
"Punitsuki G has appeared!"
But it's calling for backup though!

00:12:42.660 --> 00:12:44.040
"Akatsuki also called for allies!"
Puni!

00:12:44.040 --> 00:12:46.580
"Akatsuki also called for allies!"
He can call for backup, too?!

00:12:46.580 --> 00:12:49.370
"Punitsuki H has appeared!"
--Puni!
--Ain't that an enemy?!

00:12:49.370 --> 00:12:52.120
"Punitsuki H has appeared!"
Would you stop making them multiply?!

00:12:52.120 --> 00:12:57.370
"The Punitsukis are
doing something?"

00:12:57.370 --> 00:12:58.830
"Punitsukis become King Punitsuki."
Puni!

00:13:04.290 --> 00:13:07.250
"King Punitsuki's eyes look your way
as if begging to be friends."

00:13:20.950 --> 00:13:22.330
"Akatsuki and King Punitsuki become friends!"

00:13:22.330 --> 00:13:24.830
"Akatsuki and King Punitsuki become friends!"
Don't make him your friend!

00:13:27.620 --> 00:13:30.410
What the hell is wrong with this game?

00:13:30.410 --> 00:13:34.000
I'm tired of making wise cracks. My head hurts.

00:13:34.000 --> 00:13:35.950
There's a vending machine, right?

00:13:35.950 --> 00:13:38.250
It's packed with Paka Juice though.

00:13:38.250 --> 00:13:40.540
Seriously?

00:13:40.540 --> 00:13:44.250
That King Punitsuki was incredibly cute.

00:13:44.250 --> 00:13:46.870
All right, let's keep this going!

00:13:48.040 --> 00:13:52.200
One, two, three, four!

00:13:52.200 --> 00:13:53.370
Huh?

00:14:06.080 --> 00:14:08.040
How about you, Zak?

00:14:08.040 --> 00:14:09.790
I've got none left.

00:14:09.790 --> 00:14:12.330
Onigasaki was on a winning streak though.

00:14:12.330 --> 00:14:14.330
I'm curious to see what he's got!

00:14:14.330 --> 00:14:17.080
Yeah, check this out.

00:14:17.080 --> 00:14:18.750
He exchanged his coins...

00:14:18.750 --> 00:14:22.790
And for canned fish?
What kind of fish freak is he?

00:14:22.790 --> 00:14:24.830
What sort of canned fish is it?

00:14:24.830 --> 00:14:26.620
"Canned Paka"
Neigh.

00:14:31.290 --> 00:14:32.700
We've got trouble!

00:14:35.370 --> 00:14:38.580
I-It's Iride!

00:14:38.580 --> 00:14:41.000
Ow, ow, ow...

00:14:41.000 --> 00:14:43.540
Did I land on a pitfall trap?

00:14:50.700 --> 00:14:52.200
Akki!

00:14:52.200 --> 00:14:54.540
Where the hell did he go?

00:14:54.540 --> 00:14:57.540
If you mean Iride, he's alive and well.

00:14:57.540 --> 00:15:00.500
Thank goodness! He'll be back, right?

00:15:00.500 --> 00:15:04.000
Yes, of course. However...

00:15:05.910 --> 00:15:10.830
This bonus stage has a set time limit.

00:15:10.830 --> 00:15:12.790
But as for this pitfall trap,

00:15:12.790 --> 00:15:18.290
it was designed so that it would
be somewhat difficult to escape.

00:15:21.200 --> 00:15:28.160
All is well as long as Iride returns
before the time limit, but...

00:15:28.160 --> 00:15:31.200
What happens if he goes past the time limit?

00:15:31.200 --> 00:15:37.250
Rest assured. His life will not be
in danger if that's what you're asking.

00:15:37.250 --> 00:15:42.160
However, it means he will not
be able to return to your side.

00:15:42.160 --> 00:15:44.870
He'll become a dropout?

00:15:44.870 --> 00:15:45.700
You bastard!

00:15:45.700 --> 00:15:47.450
Cut it out, Anboy.

00:15:47.450 --> 00:15:51.450
Every second we stand here,
the time limit slowly approaches.

00:15:51.450 --> 00:15:55.000
We should be thinking about
how to bring Akki back.

00:15:57.870 --> 00:16:03.290
What if someone else played the
Dice Game and fell into the hole, too?

00:16:03.290 --> 00:16:06.160
It's dangerous, but that
might be the only way.

00:16:06.160 --> 00:16:08.750
The person with the most coins left is...

00:16:12.160 --> 00:16:13.290
Me?!

